WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:04.353
Welcome to R&D Tax Workbench NZ! In this walkthrough, we'll prepare a complete New Zealand

00:04.353 --> 00:08.107
R&D tax credit claim for Harrier Bioplastics, from sign-up to the supplementary return

00:08.107 --> 00:11.860
workpaper. Let's dive in!

00:13.867 --> 00:18.767
Getting started takes seconds. Create an account with your name, your email and a password.

00:24.447 --> 00:26.387
Confirm the password, and you're in.

00:28.767 --> 00:32.827
The AI features, like narratives and account classification, run on credits. Open the

00:32.827 --> 00:36.887
credit meter, choose a top-up, and pay securely through Stripe.

00:39.167 --> 00:41.207
Enter your card details and pay.

00:55.700 --> 00:59.090
Payment confirmed, and the credits land in your balance straight away.

01:03.226 --> 01:05.781
Create a new claim. Enter the entity name and IRD number, then the balance date and the

01:05.781 --> 01:08.336
tax year.

01:09.786 --> 01:14.276
The key deadlines appear straight away. The general approval application is due by the

01:14.276 --> 01:18.766
last day of the 3rd month after your balance date, the 30th of June here.

01:19.166 --> 01:22.561
Next come the eligibility questions under section LY 3, like a New Zealand fixed establishment,

01:22.561 --> 01:25.956
and who owns the results.

01:26.356 --> 01:28.696
Add the business address and create the claim.

01:32.796 --> 01:37.426
The entity page keeps the details and the eligible entity tests together for your file.

01:47.973 --> 01:51.123
Now the R&D project. The AI project setup works from your own notes. Paste them in, and

01:51.123 --> 01:54.273
it drafts the project for you.

02:00.653 --> 02:03.278
It proposes the core and supporting activities, and points out what Inland Revenue will

02:03.278 --> 02:05.903
look for.

02:12.373 --> 02:15.443
Two core activities, the pilot extrusion trials, and the overseas tank trials in Brisbane

02:15.443 --> 02:18.513
as a supporting activity.

02:18.913 --> 02:23.223
Create the project, and the narrative for every activity is written in one go.

02:24.961 --> 02:29.731
All the narratives are ready. Here's the project with its core and supporting activities.

02:30.131 --> 02:34.611
One section runs over the app's length limit, so condense it in a couple of clicks.

02:53.651 --> 02:56.921
Record the general approval. This one is already approved, so add the reference, the years

02:56.921 --> 03:00.191
covered and the field of research.

03:19.691 --> 03:23.181
Every activity has its full narrative, ready to review and edit.

03:47.091 --> 03:50.511
The overseas trials are a supporting activity performed outside New Zealand, which matters

03:50.511 --> 03:53.931
for the 10% overseas cap.

03:58.611 --> 04:01.131
And the narratives can be exported at any time.

04:06.765 --> 04:09.805
Payroll next. Upload the payroll file, and AI maps the columns: gross salary, PAYE, employer

04:09.805 --> 04:12.845
KiwiSaver and ESCT.

04:25.325 --> 04:28.875
A quick quality check, then import. Seven employees are loaded.

04:34.165 --> 04:36.935
Now the timesheet. The smart parser reads each person's R&D hours and matches them to

04:36.935 --> 04:39.705
the activities.

04:46.085 --> 04:48.825
Review the mappings. Sam works part time, so his R&D share is based on the hours he actually

04:48.825 --> 04:51.565
worked.

04:54.885 --> 04:58.250
The combined view brings it together: each person's salary and KiwiSaver, apportioned

04:58.250 --> 05:01.615
by R&D time across the activities.

05:02.015 --> 05:04.895
Grace has no R&D time, so nothing of hers is claimed.

05:09.424 --> 05:12.109
Now the financials. Upload the general ledger, and its twenty-four accounts are parsed

05:12.109 --> 05:14.794
and checked.

05:18.864 --> 05:21.979
Import it, and AI classifies every account against the New Zealand rules, with its reasoning,

05:21.979 --> 05:25.094
ready for your review.

05:29.024 --> 05:31.459
Loan interest, the building extension and the core technology licence are excluded by

05:31.459 --> 05:33.894
law.

05:34.294 --> 05:37.234
Review the table, then upload the trial balance separately. Each source is stored and

05:37.234 --> 05:40.174
reconciled on its own.

05:53.101 --> 05:57.221
42 trial balance accounts, ready to reconcile against the ledger.

05:59.581 --> 06:02.581
Then the profit and loss statement and the balance sheet.

06:26.741 --> 06:30.161
This ledger is an expense-only extract, so mark it as partial.

06:34.941 --> 06:39.094
AI has already marked the R&D items and chosen a category for each, so you just review

06:39.094 --> 06:43.247
its choices. Bank fees aren't R&D, so take them out, and the Raman Advisory and Brisbane

06:43.247 --> 06:47.401
lab costs are contract R&D, so set them to contractors.

07:13.546 --> 07:18.026
Apportionment. Choose a reasonable basis for each cost category, and record why.

07:20.866 --> 07:23.981
Salaries follow the timesheets. Other costs can use floor space, the FTE ratio, machine

07:23.981 --> 07:27.096
hours or direct allocation.

07:27.496 --> 07:32.346
The lab and pilot line use 252 of 420 m², so 60% of the rent. The extruder log gives 80%

07:32.346 --> 07:37.196
for depreciation.

07:46.696 --> 07:50.046
The pilot line's energy is metered separately, so it's allocated directly. Every choice

07:50.046 --> 07:53.396
has a note, ready for Inland Revenue.

07:53.796 --> 07:56.866
The comparison shows how each method affects the credit.

08:02.113 --> 08:04.918
Contractors. The ledger has three contractor accounts. Record each one, so the New Zealand

08:04.918 --> 08:07.723
rules apply.

08:08.123 --> 08:12.913
Canterbury Polymer Research Institute is an approved research provider. Its spend counts

08:12.913 --> 08:17.703
even below the $50,000 minimum, and sits outside the refundability cap.

08:36.123 --> 08:41.163
The Brisbane lab did its work overseas, so it falls under the 10% cap for foreign R&D.

08:50.203 --> 08:54.313
Raman Advisory is owned by our chief scientist, so it's an associated person and only

08:54.313 --> 08:58.423
its cost counts: $42,000 of the $60,000 invoiced.

09:01.363 --> 09:05.593
Link each contractor to the activities it worked on, as evidence for the claim.

09:41.043 --> 09:43.848
The app spots that Raman's split doesn't match the claimable amount at cost, and auto-fix

09:43.848 --> 09:46.653
rebalances it.

09:57.972 --> 10:01.757
Other expenses. Materials, overheads and depreciation are claimed here, while interest,

10:01.757 --> 10:05.542
buildings and the technology licence stay excluded.

10:10.852 --> 10:14.892
Feedstock. The surplus pilot pellets sold for $120,000, so the $76,000 of resin and energy

10:14.892 --> 10:18.932
inputs is excluded.

10:24.292 --> 10:27.122
A government grant also funded part of the project.

10:31.858 --> 10:36.508
Spend funded by the grant is ineligible, so the full $100,000 comes out.

10:41.191 --> 10:44.281
Before the summary, the reconciliation check flagged the trial balance, so line its classifications

10:44.281 --> 10:47.371
up with the ledger.

10:54.231 --> 10:57.711
Enter this year's income tax, PAYE and ESCT, and elect a refund.

11:07.624 --> 11:13.599
The summary. Eligible expenditure is $854,000, after the grant, the feedstock and the

11:13.599 --> 11:19.574
associate's margin come out. At 15%, the credit is $128,000.

11:19.974 --> 11:22.389
It first meets this year's tax, and the rest is refunded, within the PAYE, ESCT and FBT

11:22.389 --> 11:24.804
cap.

11:25.204 --> 11:27.514
And every deadline for the year is listed.

11:30.757 --> 11:34.062
The accounting page suggests the journals under NZ IAS 12, and notes the imputation credit,

11:34.062 --> 11:37.367
ready for your accountant.

11:39.457 --> 11:43.701
Outputs. The general approval is already in, so the draft checklist is tucked away. Add

11:43.701 --> 11:47.944
the contact, and the prior year's R&D spend for Inland Revenue's evaluation question.

11:47.944 --> 11:52.187
That's zero if there wasn't any, and it doesn't change the claim.

11:52.587 --> 11:55.537
Download the supplementary return workpaper in Excel.

11:57.524 --> 12:01.364
And the general approval draft in Word, for a new project or a variation.

12:09.657 --> 12:14.327
That's a complete New Zealand R&D tax credit claim, from ledgers and timesheets to the

12:14.327 --> 12:18.997
return workpaper. Thanks so much for watching, and find out more at rdinnovate.com.
